deployment:
  target: https://yawn.bot/
  mechanism: "Vercel deploys main; the pull request's Vercel Preview Comments check reported success"
  observation: not-observed-from-agent-environment
  boundary: >
    The agent's egress proxy denies connections to yawn.bot, so no browser,
    curl, or fetch from this environment could reach production. This is a
    boundary receipt, not a failure.
  what_closes_it: >
    Open https://yawn.bot/ or any Yawn page, press the participants pill in
    the header, and see the closed line "Standard · yawn.bot · 11 judgments".
    Opened, it shows @dave, 2026-09-12, rendered by @claude, the inheriting
    coordinate, the source sha256 8377bfee7824, and eleven rows. If it is
    absent, the deployment has not followed main yet or has failed; roll back
    with the merge-yawn-bot rollback line if it renders wrongly.

proof_completed:
  - "both pull requests merged by merge commit with the expected head pinned"
  - "both merge commits present on main and fetched locally"
  - "the protocol repository's check passed on the pull request and on main"
  - "the ruling is preserved verbatim and hash-bound in the approval record and quoted in the accepted review record"
  - "every rollback is one command and every branch is retained"

remaining_lacunas:
  - "production rendering is unobserved by the agent; Dave or a later session with egress can close it"
  - "the private repository's Actions runners do not start; that predates this work and is not fixed by it"
  - "no falsifier has run; the standard's rows stay asserted, reasoned, or testable"

